The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms indicating the effect of Nano-11 on the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs). When DCs were incubated with Nano-11 (black line), there was a modest increase in CD40 expression, but a marked increase in the expression of both CD80 and CD86 compared to the medium control (gray line). This demonstrates that Nano-11 activates DCs by upregulating key costimulatory molecules, which is essential for triggering an effective immune response, aligning with the PDF's findings on Nano-11's adjuvant properties.